# Guartrix daemon env — template

Paths differ by install type:

| Install | Config file | Data dir |
|---------|-------------|----------|
| Full panel / local daemon | `$INSTALL_DIR/data/daemon.env` (e.g. `/opt/guartrix/data/daemon.env`) | usually `$INSTALL_DIR/data` |
| Remote daemon-only (`install-daemon.sh` / Add node) | **`/var/lib/guartrix/daemon.env`** | `/var/lib/guartrix` |

Remote systemd units load `EnvironmentFile=/var/lib/guartrix/daemon.env`. Editing `/opt/guartrix/data/daemon.env` on a remote node has **no effect**.

Local / checkout recipe:

```bash
mkdir -p data
cp data/daemon.env.example data/daemon.env
# fill DAEMON_TOKEN + DAEMON_NODE_ID from the panel, then start the daemon
```

Remote nodes: prefer the panel wizard or `install-daemon.sh` (writes `/var/lib/guartrix/daemon.env` for you).

DAEMON_TOKEN=
DAEMON_NODE_ID=
DAEMON_PORT=8081
DAEMON_HOST=0.0.0.0
DATA_DIR=./data
PUBLIC_HOST=node1.example.com
PUBLIC_IP=
PANEL_URL=https://panel.example.com
SFTP_PORT=2022
SFTP_ENABLED=true
DOCKER_IMAGE=eclipse-temurin:25-jre-jammy
# Game container Docker json-file log rotation
# DOCKER_LOG_MAX_SIZE=10m
# DOCKER_LOG_MAX_FILE=3
# Optional Docker seccomp profile path for game containers (advanced hardening)
# DOCKER_SECCOMP_PROFILE=/path/to/seccomp.json
# Per-IP HTTP rate limit on the daemon API (default 600 requests per 60s window)
# DAEMON_RATE_LIMIT_MAX=600
# DAEMON_RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS=60000
# Game container networks (default: per_server):
#   per_server — isolated `guartrix-s-<id>` per server (recommended for multi-tenant / untrusted players);
#                daemon still attaches shared `guartrix` for game MySQL DNS (`guartrix-mysql`)
#   shared     — all game containers on flat `guartrix` bridge (simplest; good for single-tenant)
# DOCKER_NETWORK_MODE=per_server
MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=
MYSQL_PORT=3306
MYSQL_IMAGE=mysql:8.4
# Short-lived HS256 JWTs signed with DAEMON_TOKEN.
DAEMON_JWT_TTL=900
DAEMON_JWT_WS_TTL=3600
DAEMON_JWT_LEGACY=false
# Prometheus scrape (same as panel .env). Unset = localhost-only for GET /metrics.
# METRICS_TOKEN=
# Optional Sentry (daemon)
# SENTRY_DSN=
